.TH mouser 1  "mouser 1.3.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mouser \- Mouser terminal emulator
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmouser\fR [\fB\-e\fR|\fB\-\-command\fR] [\fB\-\-working\-directory\fR] [\fB\-T\fR|\fB\-\-title\fR] [\fB\-\-class\fR] [\fB\-\-hold\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-install\fR] [\fB\-\-wait\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fICMD\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Mouser terminal emulator
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-command\fR \fI<CMD>...\fR
Run a command instead of the login shell; everything after it is its arguments
.TP
\fB\-\-working\-directory\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Start in this directory instead of $HOME
.TP
\fB\-T\fR, \fB\-\-title\fR \fI<TITLE>\fR
Window title (until the program sets its own)
.TP
\fB\-\-class\fR \fI<CLASS>\fR
Wayland app_id / X11 WM_CLASS (default "Mouser")
.TP
\fB\-\-hold\fR
Keep the window open after the command exits
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to TOML config
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR \fI<CONFIG_DIR>\fR
Override config dir (tests/manual runs)
.TP
\fB\-\-install\fR \fI<SRC>\fR
Install a plugin or engine in the background once Mouser starts (repeatable; SRC as for `mouser plugin install`); see docs/downloads.md
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\fR
With \-\-install: install without a window, then exit (asks nothing: pass \-\-yes)
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
With \-\-install \-\-wait: install without asking
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fICMD\fR]
Command to run, after `\-\-` (same as \-e)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
mouser\-shell\-integration(1)
Print the shell integration for zsh, bash or fish (directory reports and silent `cd` from commander; fuzzball docs/shell.md). Load it from your rc file: `eval "$(mouser shell\-integration zsh)"`, `eval "$(mouser shell\-integration bash)"` or `mouser shell\-integration fish | source`
.TP
mouser\-show(1)
Show images in this terminal (Fuzzball graphics, or Kitty graphics as a fallback; works in tmux with allow\-passthrough)
.TP
mouser\-md(1)
Render Markdown into this terminal (headings, emphasis, code, lists, quotes, tables, OSC 8 links); see docs/markdown.md
.TP
mouser\-engine(1)
Manage GPU rendering engines (mouser, skia, custom); the same as `mouser plugin … \-\-kind engine` (engines are plugins); see docs/engines.md
.TP
mouser\-downloads(1)
The download manager\*(Aqs jobs in the running Mouser (installs and updates); `\-\-cancel ID` stops one; see docs/downloads.md
.TP
mouser\-mcp(1)
Mouser\*(Aqs MCP server (tabs, screen, shell, files for MCP clients); see docs/mcp.md
.TP
mouser\-model(1)
Model providers (OpenAI\-compatible, Anthropic, Google, local); see docs/models.md
.TP
mouser\-default\-terminal(1)
Windows: make Mouser the default terminal for console programs (docs/windows.md §Default terminal). Needs Windows Terminal installed
.TP
mouser\-help(1)
Show a help topic: the guides in docs/, built in (`mouser help` lists them, `mouser help search WORDS` finds them; a command name shows its usage); see docs/help.md
.TP
mouser\-man(1)
Write the man pages (mouser.1 and one per subcommand) into DIR; see docs/cli.md
.TP
mouser\-plugin(1)
Manage plugins (mode, model\-provider, tool\-provider, command; engines too); see docs/plugins.md
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.mouser/config.toml
Font, colours, scrollback, compression, engines, models, MCP and plugin settings (TOML).
.TP
.I ~/.mouser/preferences.toml
Choices made in the app: theme, engine order, sidebar, last mode.
.TP
.I ~/.mouser/themes/
Built-in themes, written on first run or copied on edit.
.TP
.I ~/.mouser/plugins/
Installed plugins (modes, engines, model and tool providers, commands).
.TP
.I ~/.mouser/models/
Local model weights (see MOUSER_MODELS_DIR).
.PP
The root moves with \fBMOUSER_HOME\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MOUSER_ENGINE_DIRS
Folders of engines shipped with Mouser (a path list), replacing engines/ beside the executable; empty: none (docs/engines.md).
.TP
.B MOUSER_OFFLINE_BUNDLE
Folder with the offline bundle's plugins.lock archives, instead of plugins/ beside the executable (docs/downloads.md).
.TP
.B MOUSER_CARGO
cargo used for `install crate:NAME` (default cargo; needs cargo\-binstall).
.TP
.B MOUSER_HOME
Root directory instead of ~/.mouser (config, themes, plugins, models, logs).
.TP
.B MOUSER_ENGINE
Rendering engine for this run (mouser, skia or a custom engine's name), ahead of the saved priority order.
.TP
.B MOUSER_RENDERER
cpu: draw with the CPU renderer instead of a GPU engine.
.TP
.B MOUSER_PROC_FORK
0: keep the sessions and the window in one process (no session server / UI split; Unix).
.TP
.B MOUSER_UI
headless: run the session server without a window (tests).
.TP
.B MOUSER_SYSTEM_DARK
1 or 0: whether the desktop prefers dark, overriding detection.
.TP
.B MOUSER_OPEN_SIDEBAR
Open the sidebar for this run, whatever was saved.
.TP
.B MOUSER_MODELS_DIR
Where local model weights live (before [models.local] dir and <home>/models).
.TP
.B MOUSER_MODEL_URL_OVERRIDE
Download URL for `mouser model download` instead of the pinned one.
.TP
.B MOUSER_GROKBOT_HOME
Grok Bot desktop home used by `mouser model add grok \-\-desktop` (default: the app's own).
.TP
.B MOUSER_GROK_POLL_MS
Poll interval in ms for the grok Cursor\-agents and desktop providers.
.TP
.B MOUSER_SECRET_STORE
file: keep API keys and tokens in a 0600 file under <home> instead of the OS keychain.
.TP
.B MOUSER_SSH_BIN
ssh binary for remote commander and the connection manager (default ssh).
.TP
.B MOUSER_SSH_CONFIG
SSH config Mouser reads and edits (default ~/.ssh/config).
.TP
.B MOUSER_REMOTE_BACKEND
rsync, scp or cat: force how remote files are fetched.
.TP
.B MOUSER_PLAYER_LOG
Write the media player's log to this file.
.TP
.B MOUSER_LLM_TIMINGS
Print llama.cpp timings for the built\-in local model.
.TP
.B MOUSER_PLUGIN_DIRS
extra plugin folders (a path list), replacing the offline bundle and system folders; empty: only $MOUSER_HOME/plugins (docs/plugins.md).
.TP
.B MOUSER_MODE_WIRE
json: mode plugins (mouser\-mode\-api) speak JSON instead of MessagePack on stdio, for debugging (docs/mode\-protocol.md).
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log filter (env_logger), e.g. debug or mouser=trace.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 on an error (the message goes to stderr); 2 for a usage error.
.SH SECURITY
API keys and MCP tokens are kept in the OS keychain (or a 0600 file with MOUSER_SECRET_STORE=file) and are never printed or logged.
Pass keys on stdin (\fB\-\-key\-stdin\fR), not as arguments. The MCP server listens on 127.0.0.1 unless \fBbind\fR is set, and then only over HTTPS with a token.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
mouser \-e btop
mouser \-\-working\-directory ~/src \-\- nvim .
mouser show photo.png
mouser md README.md
printf %s "$XAI_KEY" | mouser model add grok \-\-key\-stdin
mouser mcp cert status
mouser default\-terminal set
mouser help models
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmouser help\fR (the built-in guides), https://mouser.weirdbrains.com
